Hello Jeff,

As discussed in a recent thread [1], my QCA9377 chipset device also
exhibits poor performance when PMF is negotiated either in WPA2-PSK or
WPA3-SAE modes, which can be resolved by setting the mfp-support
firmware feature flag. The reason for this is assumed to be identical to
Shunsuke Nagashima's discovery [2] re: the WCN3990 firmware sending
unprotected ADDBA Request frames.

My device came included with a Dell Inspiron 5570 which identifies as a
hw1.1 revision pci device, but it uses the standard QCA9377/hw1.0
firmware(s):

qca9377 hw1.1 target 0x05020001 chip_id 0x003821ff sub 1028:1810
WLAN.TF.2.1-00021-QCARMSWP-1 api 6 features wowlan,ignore-otp crc32
42e41877
WLAN.TF.1.0-00002-QCATFSWPZ-5 api 5 features ignore-otp crc32
c3e0d04f

As per the recommendation from Loic, I am attaching the modified
firmware files for consideration. The exact reproduction steps are as
follows using the latest [3] [4] firmware blobs for my chipset.

$ mkdir -p original modified
$ cp -a ~/work/linux-firmware/ath10k/QCA9377/hw1.0/firmware-5.bin \
original/
$ cp -a ~/work/linux-firmware/ath10k/QCA9377/hw1.0/firmware-6.bin \
original/
$ cp -a original/*.bin modified/

$ ./ath10k-fwencoder --dump-cmdline --show-timestamp \
original/firmware-6.bin

(output) ath10k-fwencoder --create \
--firmware-version=WLAN.TF.2.1-00021-QCARMSWP-1 \
--timestamp=1536825307 \
--features=wowlan,ignore-otp-result \
--firmware=athwlan.bin \
--otp=otp.bin \
--set-wmi-op-version=tlv \
--set-htt-op-version=tlv \

$ ./ath10k-fwencoder --modify \
--features=wowlan,ignore-otp-result,mfp-support \
--timestamp=1536825307 \
modified/firmware-6.bin

(output) modified/firmware-6.bin modified: 751436 B

$ ./ath10k-fwencoder --dump-cmdline --show-timestamp \
original/firmware-5.bin

(output) ath10k-fwencoder --create \
