I verified these results against my ISP router (Virgin Media Hub 5x) and
a different OpenWrt router with an IPQ5018/QCN6122 chipset via ath11k.

Benchmark result taken from api 6 firmware, but api 5 firmware was also
confirmed to have the same issue and resolution on my device, even
though I don't plan to actually use the older api 5 firmware myself.

The unmodified firmwares can also both reach ~250-300Mbps, but only if
connected via WPA2-PSK with PMF disabled (achieved by setting my router
to WPA3 Transition Mode and forcing PMF disabled on the client). Windows
can reach a similar ~250-300Mbps without any issues when PMF is active.

